# Compact Policy

Compact only at major workflow boundaries after durable project context is written.

## Source Of Truth

- `AGENTS.md`
- `.planning/STATE.md`
- `.planning/phases/`
- `.planning/checkpoints/`
- `openspec/`
- git diff and log

## Instruction

When a checkpoint reports `compact_status: pending`, run `/compact` in Codex CLI before continuing in the
current thread. When a checkpoint reports `compact_status: not_needed`, the task is at a stopping point and
state is already updated; compact is optional before starting a new thread or using the checkpoint as handoff
context.

When an external API or harness runs compaction for a pending gate, record the returned payload with `record_compact_result.py`.
The compact record is evidence for the gate; repository files remain the source of truth.
